cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset in teaching or research, please cite it as below. All data are synthetic."
type: dataset
title: "Synthetic Dataset for Visual Communication Education and Research"
abstract: >-
  SynthVisCom is an open synthetic dataset for teaching and researching
  visual communication. 2,000 simulated designs (posters, infographics, data
  charts, social media images and slides) are described by colour, contrast,
  typography, layout, hierarchy and image-to-text ratio, each with a PNG
  image drawn from its variables, and are seen by 1,000 simulated
  participants who produce 20,000 responses on attention, comprehension,
  recall, aesthetics, preference, cognitive load and engagement. A codebook,
  a data descriptor, the documented generating effects and a reproducible
  base-R generator and renderer are included, so analyses can be checked
  against a known truth. All data are synthetic and do not
  represent real people, designs or empirical findings. Data and
  documentation are released under CC BY 4.0 and code under the MIT License.
